00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, you know,
is a sovereign nation

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.577 line:92%
but in many ways a bad actor

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:13.747
How do you -- would you
go about, if you were president,

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:16.850
trying to deescalate
the current situation with Iran?

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.618 line:92%
-Well, you know, the first job

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:23.356
of the President of the United
States is to keep America safe

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:27.961
And this President has gone in
exactly the opposite direction

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:30.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he started in
three years ago

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:33.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
when he tore up
the Iran nuclear deal

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:37.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Iran had agreed not
to advance its nuclear program

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:39.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
Our allies wanted America
to stay in it,

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:42.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
but instead, Donald Trump
tore it up.

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:45.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's just had
a series of escalating attacks

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:50.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now with the killing
of Soleimani, we're in a place

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:55.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
where we've stopped our action
against ISIS.

00:00:55.121 --> 00:01:03.129
We now have a president who is
tweeting threats of war crimes

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:07.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've had to pull all of
the Americans out of the area,

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.135 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
all the civilians.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is not
making America safer.

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:13.973
And what it's really doing, we
really have to talk about this

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:19.546 size:88% position:44%
this is moving us closer
to the very edge of war.

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:24.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
Americans don't want
a war with Iran.

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:25.118 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And this is the moment

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:28.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
Americans need to speak up
need to speak up loudly

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:31.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
and say no more war
in the Middle East.

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:33.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's time to have
peace in the Middle East.

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
We need to get out of this
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:40.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It does seem like
we're living in an era

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:43.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
where there is an expansio
of presidential powers.

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:47.974
You know, Congress has les
to say about what wars we're in,

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:49.509 line:92%
how those wars are fought.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:52.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, from Presiden
Obama to President Trump,

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:54.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
